cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this workflow, please cite it using the metadata below. Please also cite the underlying methods listed in docs/11_references.md."
title: "MultiSampleSomaticWorkflow (MSSW): a GATK4+ WDL pipeline for somatic variant, copy-number, and clonal analysis"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Hähnel"
    given-names: "Philipp"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9584-9135"
    affiliation: "Mass General Brigham"
abstract: >-
  The MultiSampleSomaticWorkflow (MSSW) is a WDL pipeline for somatic analysis of
  tissue or liquid biopsy samples from cancer patients. It assumes DNA data and
  supports WES, WGS, and panel sequencing. Built on GATK4, it covers preprocessing,
  single nucleotide variant (SNV) calling, copy number variation (CNV) calling, and
  clonal analysis (ABSOLUTE, PhylogicNDT).
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-04"
license: "BSD-3-Clause"
repository-code: "https://github.com/phylyc/somatic_workflow"
url: "https://phylyc.github.io/somatic_workflow/"
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - somatic-variant-calling
  - copy-number-variation
  - WDL
  - GATK4
  - cancer-genomics
  - WES
  - WGS
